{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1782045297727,"sessionID":"ses_115d2c415ffeIpCcJo4jsm7TNT","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_5fad6673aaf742ca8aa1fabe","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-xt4_kqgs/retort-9639bd9e98e3/TASK.md"},"output":"<path>/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-xt4_kqgs/retort-9639bd9e98e3/TASK.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: Create a REST API service for managing a book collection.\n2: \n3: Requirements:\n4: - POST /books — Create a new book (title, author, year, isbn)\n5: - GET /books — List all books (support ?author= filter)\n6: - GET /books/{id} — Get a single book by ID\n7: - PUT /books/{id} — Update a book\n8: - DELETE /books/{id} — Delete a book\n9: \n10: Technical constraints:\n11: - Use the specified language and framework\n12: - Store data in SQLite (or language-equivalent embedded DB)\n13: - Return JSON responses with appropriate HTTP status codes\n14: - Include input validation (title and author are required)\n15: - Include a health check endpoint: GET /health\n16: \n17: Deliverables:\n18: - Working source code in the workspace directory\n19: - A README.md with setup and run instructions\n20: - At least 3 unit/integration tests\n\n(End of file - total 20 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"Create a REST API service for managing a book collection.\n\nRequirements:\n- POST /books — Create a new book (title, author, year, isbn)\n- GET /books — List all books (support ?author= filter)\n- GET /books/{id} — Get a single book by ID\n- PUT /books/{id} — Update a book\n- DELETE /books/{id} — Delete a book\n\nTechnical constraints:\n- Use the specified language and framework\n- Store data in SQLite (or language-equivalent embedded DB)\n- Return JSON responses with appropriate HTTP status codes\n- Include input validation (title and author are required)\n- Include a health check endpoint: GET /hea